  "published": "2026-07-27T11:26:13.58Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.4.0 — Request logging no longer reports Error for failures that are not the application's. Fixed: a client-aborted request (closed tab, reload, dropped connection) was logged at Error, which triggered step-up and flushed the pre-error buffer — on an anonymous route any caller could do that just by disconnecting. Such a request is now logged at Information; a genuine exception on an also-aborted request is still Error. Added: `TreatServerErrorStatusAsError` (default true, today's behaviour) — set it to false in a reverse proxy or BFF so a status >= 500 with no exception is logged at Warning instead of Error, keeping backend-relayed 5xx out of the step-up trigger path. Fixes #17. No public API break.",
